&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49720015</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 22:58:53 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Has anyone made any money/successes making SaaS's with AI?</title><link>https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49719966</link><description>&lt;p&gt;I've had a few attempts on side projects throughout the years. Nothing seems to stick and now with AI it's as if everything is possible yet equates to 0 value. Can I get some feedback? What am I doing wrong? Is it just too late?&lt;p&gt;My actual public attempts so far:
cluekangaroo.com - structured homework help with clues for middleschoolers and highschoolers (I use AI, but anonymize any personal data and encrypt it all)&lt;p&gt;drawesome.art - this is a personal love project because I love drawing esp with my kids and friends I can't of way to make it make money (I think the hosting would be kind of expensive)&lt;p&gt;Catchmemeow.com - my daily game I made for my daughters to help them get dogs/cats adopted.&lt;p&gt;therapscalliongame.com - a silly fantasy game.&lt;p&gt;I just feel having the little side project that makes a little money in this day and age is over now. Everything is AI. Kind of feeling hopeless this is just me shouting into the void I'm sure. I don't want to sound spammy just want candid feedback.&lt;/p&gt;
